WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.748
- Sometimes I just buy food and put it

00:00:01.748 --> 00:00:04.284
in the fridge and just wait
for it to be left over.

00:00:04.284 --> 00:00:09.191
(competitive music)

00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:17.319
- Right off the bat, this
hot one's really good.

00:00:17.319 --> 00:00:19.669
- Something about that cheese
is real good when it's hot.

00:00:19.669 --> 00:00:21.666
- The cheese is never
gonna be as like gooey

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:23.940
and delicious as it originally was.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.592
- Solid crust?

00:00:24.592 --> 00:00:26.310
- Ah man, that's amazing.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.033
That's good.
- Just like my mama

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.506
microwaved it.

00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:30.087
- [Voiceover] This is
something that people

00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:31.553
like almost more.

00:00:31.553 --> 00:00:33.598
- There's just something so heart-warming

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:35.060
about leftover cold pizza.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.359
- It doesn't move, which is always good.

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:37.834
- Okay. Alright.
- Yeah.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.134
- It's a whole different experience.

00:00:39.134 --> 00:00:40.285
- Like sometimes if you're feeling lazy

00:00:40.285 --> 00:00:42.097
you just wanna open the
fridge and get something,

00:00:42.097 --> 00:00:44.141
but this is so much more satisfying.

00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:45.546
- I still like the cold one better.

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:46.358
- I like this one better.

00:00:46.358 --> 00:00:48.563
- To me a little more flavor will hold.

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:49.305
That's so weird.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.245
(dinging)

00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:54.434
- [Voiceover] Spaghetti,
spaghetti, spaghetti.

00:00:55.543 --> 00:00:57.143
- Yeah, it is always better a day later.

00:00:57.143 --> 00:00:58.115
I don't know why.

00:00:58.115 --> 00:01:00.228
- Put a little parmesan on it. Bam!

00:01:00.228 --> 00:01:01.343
You got yourself another meal.

00:01:01.343 --> 00:01:02.337
- [Voiceover] Who eats cold spaghetti?

00:01:02.337 --> 00:01:03.231
That's not a thing.

00:01:03.231 --> 00:01:05.357
- I hands down eat cold spaghetti.

00:01:06.998 --> 00:01:08.410
- I hate this.
- Whoa.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.535
- I think there's maybe a
texture, slimy thing happening.

00:01:11.535 --> 00:01:12.369
- It's too cold.

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:13.612
- I'm okay with it.

00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:14.587
- I don't like it.

00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:17.513
- Well 'cause it's cold spaghetti. Duh.

00:01:17.513 --> 00:01:19.254
- You can't skimp on the
microwave on this one.

00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:19.632
- No.

00:01:19.632 --> 00:01:21.949
- I'll eat your cold noodles.
- Yeah, go for it.

00:01:21.949 --> 00:01:23.109
(dinging)

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:26.392
- [Voiceover] Shrimp Pad Thai.

00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:28.819
- Hot leftover Thai is
just a familiar friend.

00:01:28.819 --> 00:01:30.097
- Okay. Good.

00:01:31.349 --> 00:01:32.232
- That's really great.

00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:33.706
The microwave actually helps this.

00:01:33.706 --> 00:01:34.819
- [Voiceover] I feel
like I might be getting

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:36.012
a little more flavor on the cold.

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.577
- It's kind of just dancing.

00:01:37.577 --> 00:01:39.620
- There's a civil war
happening in your mouth.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.708
- Not bad.
- It's not bad.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:42.937
- If I have the opportunity to go two feet

00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:44.608
to my left and put it in the microwave,

00:01:44.608 --> 00:01:45.747
I'm definitely going to take that.

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:47.556
- If I had this already the night before,

00:01:47.556 --> 00:01:50.495
I might wanna switch it up
and have cold the next day.

00:01:50.495 --> 00:01:51.970
- You can't eat Thai food cold.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.153
Like, we told y'all that.

00:01:53.153 --> 00:01:54.071
- My mom told me.

00:01:54.071 --> 00:01:55.700
- Your mom's wrong.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.885
(dinging)

00:01:58.958 --> 00:01:59.685
- [Voiceover] Vegetable lo mein.

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:00.812
- Yeah, this is good.

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:01.832
- This is like college.

00:02:01.832 --> 00:02:03.529
- The heated up one's just like dry.

00:02:03.529 --> 00:02:06.152
- They kind of just like flatten
out and you're like- (gags)

00:02:06.152 --> 00:02:07.742
- There's no way this
can compete with this.

00:02:07.742 --> 00:02:08.192
- Let's see though.

00:02:08.192 --> 00:02:09.758
- [Voiceover] I think we're
gonna get into some territory

00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:11.288
where the cold doesn't fly.

00:02:11.288 --> 00:02:13.086
- The cold one was sloppy.

00:02:13.086 --> 00:02:13.980
- Whoa.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.969
- I think the cold one's
- Weird

00:02:14.969 --> 00:02:15.769
makes it sweeter.

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:16.942
- I actually think I was way wrong.

00:02:16.942 --> 00:02:17.775
It's totally fine.

00:02:17.775 --> 00:02:18.449
- That's great.

00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:20.433
- Whoa, my mind is blown.
- I don't know if I-

00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:21.688
- Cold is awesome.

00:02:21.688 --> 00:02:23.836
- This one's better 'cause it's hot.

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:25.716
But I see the appeal for this one too.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:27.515
(dinging)

00:02:29.287 --> 00:02:30.692
- [Voiceover] Classic.
People eat Thanksgiving

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:32.007
leftovers for weeks.

00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:32.611
- Yeah.

00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:34.365
- I mean this is the
Star Wars of leftovers.

00:02:34.365 --> 00:02:35.247
- That's delicious.

00:02:35.247 --> 00:02:37.023
- I love Thanksgiving so much.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.408
- [Voiceover] Why would you
dishonor it by not reheating it?

00:02:39.408 --> 00:02:39.866
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:41.538
- Turkey looks daunting.

00:02:41.538 --> 00:02:42.814
- Not bad.

00:02:42.814 --> 00:02:44.230
- Cold mashed potatoes, totally fine.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.449
- Are you kidding me?

00:02:45.449 --> 00:02:46.038
What is this?

00:02:46.038 --> 00:02:47.757
This is like a dirt clod.

00:02:47.757 --> 00:02:48.674
- This tastes bad.

00:02:48.674 --> 00:02:52.272
- Trying to take me to
Blandville, USA, population none.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.084
(dinging)

00:02:55.462 --> 00:02:56.381
- [Voiceover] Do whatever you gotta do

00:02:56.381 --> 00:02:57.332
to eat the damn thing.

00:02:57.332 --> 00:02:58.657
You know there's hungry people everywhere.

00:02:58.657 --> 00:03:00.234
- We're in a very privileged position

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:03.514
to be sitting here arguing
about the temperature

00:03:03.518 --> 00:03:06.445
of my leftover food
that I couldn't finish.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.122
- [Voiceover] If you're gonna
recook it in the microwave,

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.456
you don't capture the
essence of the original meal

00:03:12.456 --> 00:03:14.139
that was left over for you to eat.

00:03:14.139 --> 00:03:15.181
- That logic makes no sense.

00:03:15.181 --> 00:03:16.060
- That makes all the sense in the world.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:16.926
- It does not.

